# Cyclic p-subgroups versus roots of the modular polynomial

Definition: `ModularCurve_CycSubRootBridge` (`daa85f3b-17ec-5860-975e-25c24e3c9063`), by Claude,
2026-09-05.

Throughout, $H = \mathrm{HahnSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the Hahn-series field
with rational exponents and coefficients in an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$; `isAlgClosed_H`
and `charZero_H` record that it is algebraically closed of characteristic zero, and
`transcendental_rat_of_transcendental_qbar` transfers transcendence over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to
transcendence over $\mathbb{Q}$. For a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $H$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$, an
element of `CycSubH E N` is a subgroup $G$ of $E(H)$ together with the existence of $g \in E(H)$ of
additive order $N$ with $G = \mathbb{Z}g$; `cycSubGen` chooses such a generator,
`addOrderOf_cycSubGen` and `coe_eq_zmultiples_cycSubGen` state its two defining properties, and
`CycSubH.ext` says such data are determined by the underlying subgroup. For a prime $p \neq 2$,
`cycSubSummingSet E G` is the finite set of affine coordinate pairs of $g, 2g, \dots,
\frac{p-1}{2}g$ (Vélu summing set of odd order), and `isElliptic_veluQuotient_cycSubSummingSet`
shows the associated Vélu quotient $E/G$ has invertible discriminant. Given $\Phi$ of level $p$ (a
`ModularPolynomialData p`: a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(p)$ vanishing on the
pair $(j(q), j(q^p))$), `cycSubRoot E hp2 data G` is the element $j(E/G)$ of `RootsAt data E.j`, the
subtype of $y \in H$ with $\Phi(j(E), y) = 0$ after mapping coefficients into $H$ via $X \mapsto
j(E)$. If $j(E)$ is transcendental over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ this map is injective
(`cycSubRoot_injective`). The counting part establishes $\#\,$`CycSubH E p`$\, = \psi(p) = \sum_{d
\mid p,\ d \text{ squarefree}} p/d$ (`natCard_cycSubH`, via a characterisation of the
cyclic-subgroup condition as `IsAddCyclic` together with cardinality $p$), finiteness of both sides,
and $\#\,$`RootsAt data E.j`$\, \le \psi(p)$ from $\deg_Y \Phi = \psi(p)$. Hence `cycSubRoot` is
bijective, and `rootsEquivCycSubH` is its inverse equivalence $\mathrm{RootsAt}(\Phi, j(E)) \simeq
\mathrm{CycSubH}(E,p)$, with the two computation rules $e^{-1}(G) = j(E/G)$ and $e(r) = G \iff r =
j(E/G)$.

**Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib supplies the ambient objects — `HahnSeries`, `AlgebraicClosure`,
`WeierstrassCurve` with its affine points and `AddSubgroup.zmultiples` — while the cyclic-subgroup
type `CycSubH`, the root subtype `RootsAt`, the Vélu quotient and its odd summing sets, the
modular-polynomial datum and the Dedekind $\psi$ function are the project's own definitions.

**Where it is used.** The equivalence constructed here is exactly the data required by the predicate
`ModuliDictionary` at prime level: over the Hahn-series field it identifies the roots of the
level-$p$ modular polynomial at $j(E)$ with the order-$p$ cyclic subgroups of $E$, each root being
the $j$-invariant of the corresponding Vélu quotient. This is part of the construction of modular
curves and their modular equations used in the modularity route to Fermat's Last Theorem.

